         <ResourceName>All Real-Time Shock Candidates</ResourceName>
         <ReleaseDate>2026-11-04T10:38:52</ReleaseDate>
         <Description>The All Real-Time Shock Candidates list is an automated catalog maintained by the ACE Science Center at Caltech that logs every potential interplanetary shock wave detected in real-time solar wind data from NASA&#039;s Advanced Composition Explorer (ACE) spacecraft. Unlike the filtered &quot;Good Shocks&quot; list—which only displays confirmed, high-confidence events—the All Shock Candidates list includes every triggered detection. This includes weak shocks, oblique shocks, rotational discontinuities, and false positives flagged with explanations for why a solution was inadequate.</Description>
